  "step_3": "The decision reason requires attention to the maximum loss and a preference for the lottery with the less severe loss. However, both lotteries have the same maximum loss (0 Euros), so the reason would not favor one over the other. The individual, in contrast, does not consider losses at all — their deliberation is focused on gains and the chance of achieving a higher payout. There is no evidence that losses were weighted more heavily than gains, nor that the worst outcome was a key consideration. The information used by the individual (potential gains, high probability of winning) does not align with the information required by the reason (maximum losses). The justification (pursuit of higher gain) also contradicts the rationale of loss aversion. Therefore, it is certain that the individual did not use this decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
